Z||000019||Monkeyman||12-22-1999||09:39 AM||||I was a member of another Fiero forum for a little less than a day (it sucked).  One of the messages I got had something to do with getting a dogbone chromed.  I'll try to post it here.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Monkeyman||12-22-1999||09:51 AM||||OK.  I didn't know that I couldn't post an email here, but basically it says that it's not a big deal to chrome a dogbone or anything else that's loadbearing.  The sender suggested that it shouldn't cost more than $20 or $30.  If you live in a bigger city, check in the yellow pages under "Metal Refinishing" or something like that.  Body shops or custom/speed shops might have some info, too.  I plan on keeping the original, polish it (I like polished alum better than chrome), and replace the bushings with polys.||||reg||1
Z||000021||fiero56||12-22-1999||10:23 AM||||When I got my Fiero, the dogbone was all dirty, not very smooth. I pulled out a wire wheel brush for a drill, and it got the dogbone shining again. Also worked on the EGR valve, and the rings with the tree bolts on the strut towers.<BR>Monkeyman: if you want to post an e-mail here: right click your mouse, hightlight everything you want to post, release the button and click copy on the dialog box that pops up. Then when hit sft+insert where you want to copy the text to. Sounds a little difficult, but its really not that hard.||||reg||1
Z||000022||Monkeyman||12-22-1999||03:12 PM||||Thanx.  I got everything highlighted, but didn't know where to go from there.||||reg||1
